1
00:00:01,501 --> 00:00:03,203
Just the three of us again?

2
00:00:03,269 --> 00:00:05,372
Where has Akira been going lately anyway?

3
00:00:05,438 --> 00:00:08,475
Apparently, he has been scouting
at a lot of different hospitals.

4
00:00:08,541 --> 00:00:09,542
Scouting?

5
00:00:09,609 --> 00:00:10,944
He has been complaining,

6
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:13,313
"This is a famous doctor agency,

7
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:14,948
but I have no doctors."

8
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:17,450
He missed out on getting Nurse X, too.

9
00:00:18,585 --> 00:00:21,287
What's his problem?
The three of us should be plenty!

10
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:23,089
I'll operate all he wants!

11
00:00:23,156 --> 00:00:24,958
There's your papa's girl streak.

12
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:27,127
Wait, it's more like "Akira's girl."

13
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:29,562
- I am not!
- Well, you know,

14
00:00:29,629 --> 00:00:33,233
it's not easy to find a surgeon
that can compare to you, Michiko.

15
00:00:33,299 --> 00:00:36,202
Cut that out.
Your flattering has made her goofy.

16
00:00:36,269 --> 00:00:38,905
I'm quick and good!

17
00:00:38,972 --> 00:00:40,407
<i>- Ron!</i>
- What?

18
00:00:40,473 --> 00:00:43,009
All ones and nines, read them and weep!

19
00:00:43,076 --> 00:00:45,478
That was fast! It's only our fifth draw!

20
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:47,947
- I'm quick and good!
- You're cheating!

21
00:00:48,014 --> 00:00:49,315
- What? Hey!
- You're cheating.

22
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:51,284
BEIJING

23
00:00:51,351 --> 00:00:53,820
LONG LIVE THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA

24
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,696
Are you sure it will be okay?

25
00:01:03,763 --> 00:01:05,598
Don't worry.

26
00:01:06,699 --> 00:01:10,270
Japan's best university hospital

27
00:01:10,336 --> 00:01:14,841
is already fully prepared
for receiving him.

28
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:19,679
Please leave the surgery
to our famous doctor.

29
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:23,583
- "Romantic"!
- "C"?

30
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:27,220
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

31
00:01:28,655 --> 00:01:30,390
<i>2021.</i>

32
00:01:30,890 --> 00:01:34,027
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

33
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:36,362
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

34
00:01:37,363 --> 00:01:39,299
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>

35
00:01:39,365 --> 00:01:41,634
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

36
00:01:41,701 --> 00:01:44,537
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

37
00:01:45,305 --> 00:01:46,139
<i>However,</i>

38
00:01:46,206 --> 00:01:48,241
<i>the university hospital's once illustrious</i>

39
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:51,111
<i>Surgery Department was moved</i>
<i>to the branch hospital.</i>

40
00:01:51,177 --> 00:01:54,214
<i>The number of surgeries</i>
<i>was greatly decreased</i>

41
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,716
<i>and it was running in the red.</i>

42
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:59,752
- Hey, the internists aren't here.
- You're right.

43
00:01:59,819 --> 00:02:02,722
Chief Hachisuka and his people
are traveling

44
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,858
around Asia with some politicians.

45
00:02:04,924 --> 00:02:06,059
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

46
00:02:06,126 --> 00:02:08,661
<i>this freelance maverick doctor</i>

47
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:13,333
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

48
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:16,469
Thanks for coming out to meet me.

49
00:02:16,536 --> 00:02:18,338
We're not here for you!

50
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:21,107
Oh, is a VIP patient coming?

51
00:02:21,174 --> 00:02:24,644
- Let me operate on them.
- Shut up. You greet them, too!

52
00:02:24,711 --> 00:02:26,779
- I won't!
- What? Ouch!

53
00:02:26,846 --> 00:02:27,814
That hurt!

54
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:29,749
Damn, that really hurt!

55
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:31,284
They're here!

56
00:02:31,784 --> 00:02:33,153
Quit shouting!

57
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:52,272
A child?

58
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:55,508
Mr. Miroku Oh, we've been expecting you.

59
00:02:57,210 --> 00:03:00,380
I am Hideki Kaji,
nearly the Surgery Director.

60
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:03,149
Allow me to show you inside.

61
00:03:05,885 --> 00:03:08,421
Hey, Demon! Get out of the way!

62
00:03:08,488 --> 00:03:10,123
You mean this guy is the VIP?

63
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,324
"This guy?"

64
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:13,960
Don't talk like that, you moron!

65
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:16,629
He's the son of the chairman
of China's Fenzu Group!

66
00:03:17,197 --> 00:03:18,631
"Fenzu?"

67
00:03:18,698 --> 00:03:20,099
I think I've heard of it.

68
00:03:20,166 --> 00:03:21,968
It's China's greatest IT group.

69
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,269
The chairman is Jake Wang.

70
00:03:23,336 --> 00:03:25,238
He's Asia's wealthiest man!

71
00:03:25,805 --> 00:03:27,507
Let me operate on you.

72
00:03:27,574 --> 00:03:29,375
I never make mistakes.

73
00:03:29,442 --> 00:03:31,778
Hey! Quit getting so familiar!
Out of the way!

74
00:03:31,844 --> 00:03:32,679
Did you hear me?

75
00:03:32,745 --> 00:03:34,614
- Get out of the way!
- What's your problem?

76
00:03:34,681 --> 00:03:35,615
What's your problem?

77
00:03:36,316 --> 00:03:37,450
It's okay.

78
00:03:38,818 --> 00:03:39,852
Let's go.

79
00:03:40,453 --> 00:03:41,621
Oh, he speaks Japanese.

80
00:03:42,255 --> 00:03:43,890
I am terribly sorry.

81
00:03:43,957 --> 00:03:46,559
I apologize for that stupid
and crude woman.

82
00:03:46,626 --> 00:03:48,228
This way, please.

83
00:03:53,766 --> 00:03:54,767
What?

84
00:03:55,735 --> 00:04:00,506
Please, don't worry about a thing
and leave this in our hands.

85
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:03,376
If anything at all bothers you,

86
00:04:03,443 --> 00:04:07,013
feel free to tell
any of my subordinates about it.

87
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,616
You're too high up, people!

88
00:04:09,682 --> 00:04:11,017
Yes, sir!

89
00:04:13,019 --> 00:04:14,287
Come in.

90
00:04:14,354 --> 00:04:15,488
Excuse me.

91
00:04:15,555 --> 00:04:17,724
YUI ASAGUMO
ACTING HOSPITAL DIRECTOR SECRETARY

92
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:24,197
Allow me to welcome you
with the best that I can offer.

93
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:27,734
We have prepared traditional Chinese tea.

94
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,435
Please, help yourself.

95
00:04:30,003 --> 00:04:33,840
I understand trying to please him,
but he's not the Last Emperor.

96
00:04:34,474 --> 00:04:36,342
This is Acting Director Hiruma's chance

97
00:04:36,409 --> 00:04:39,312
to build a connection
with the Fenzu Group, after all.

98
00:04:40,246 --> 00:04:42,282
While Chief Hachisuka is away,

99
00:04:42,815 --> 00:04:45,184
he's trying to achieve a great triumph.

100
00:04:46,052 --> 00:04:48,955
- He hasn't changed a bit.
- Nope, not a bit.

101
00:04:49,022 --> 00:04:50,823
Hey! It's you, Dr. Hara!

102
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:51,924
What? Dr. Hara?

103
00:04:51,991 --> 00:04:53,092
Silence!

104
00:04:53,159 --> 00:04:54,093
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

105
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,763
- Yes, I'm Dr. Hara.
- "I'm Dr. Hara?"

106
00:04:56,829 --> 00:04:59,098
You sure have changed. Don't mind that.

107
00:04:59,165 --> 00:05:01,668
At last. You're back. I've been waiting!

108
00:05:01,734 --> 00:05:04,771
I'll make the most of this chance,
so help me out.

109
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:08,574
Don't worry about the surgery.

110
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:12,879
We have magnificent facilities
and talented staff.

111
00:05:12,945 --> 00:05:14,614
- Allow me to interrupt.
- What?

112
00:05:14,681 --> 00:05:16,716
Please allow me, Hideki Kaji,

113
00:05:16,783 --> 00:05:19,585
the best surgeon
in the Surgery Department,

114
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,521
to perform the surgery.

115
00:05:22,355 --> 00:05:23,589
- Come in.
- Excuse me.

116
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:25,925
Acting Director Hiruma, they're here.

117
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:27,527
Please, let them in.

118
00:05:27,593 --> 00:05:29,395
Excuse me.

119
00:05:29,462 --> 00:05:31,798
I'm terribly sorry for being late.

120
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:37,337
I am very glad that you have
arrived safely, Miroku.

121
00:05:38,438 --> 00:05:40,039
I thought it was you, Akira.

122
00:05:40,106 --> 00:05:42,075
Hey, what are you doing here?

123
00:05:44,944 --> 00:05:51,117
Mr. Kambara here referred Miroku
to Totei University Hospital.

124
00:05:51,184 --> 00:05:52,118
Really?

125
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,253
You brought in this patient,
did you? Thanks!

126
00:05:54,754 --> 00:05:56,322
It's going to Demon?

127
00:05:56,389 --> 00:05:58,725
I'm counting on you,

128
00:05:58,791 --> 00:06:00,259
Dr. Hara.

129
00:06:00,326 --> 00:06:01,594
- What?
- What?

130
00:06:01,661 --> 00:06:02,495
Yes.

131
00:06:02,562 --> 00:06:03,663
Who are you?

132
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:07,834
I have become a member
of the Kambara Doctor Referral Agency.

133
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:10,269
I am a freelance surgeon. Mamoru Hara.

134
00:06:10,336 --> 00:06:11,704
- What?
- What?

135
00:06:12,271 --> 00:06:14,040
The year before I came here,

136
00:06:14,107 --> 00:06:18,745
I learned Chinese surgical techniques
at a Chinese hospital.

137
00:06:18,811 --> 00:06:20,980
It's nice to meet all of you.

138
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:23,182
- Akira, what's going on?
- What's with him?

139
00:06:23,249 --> 00:06:24,784
I don't know how to react.

140
00:06:24,851 --> 00:06:27,420
Miroku, don't worry.

141
00:06:27,487 --> 00:06:29,455
I'll do just as I promised in China.

142
00:06:30,757 --> 00:06:32,725
Thank you, Dr. Hara.

143
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:35,628
- I'll take care of you.
- Dr. Hara.

144
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:40,733
All the care I gave
in making you better has paid off.

145
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,235
You've really grown.

146
00:06:42,301 --> 00:06:44,370
<i>- This woman…</i>
- Magnificent!

147
00:06:44,937 --> 00:06:46,072
<i>She hates groups,</i>

148
00:06:46,139 --> 00:06:47,407
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

149
00:06:47,473 --> 00:06:48,608
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

150
00:06:49,108 --> 00:06:52,378
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

151
00:06:52,445 --> 00:06:54,347
<i>to work her way up.</i>

152
00:06:54,414 --> 00:06:56,549
Hey! Akira!

153
00:06:56,616 --> 00:06:59,552
What's going on here? Why use Kin-chan?

154
00:06:59,619 --> 00:07:01,421
Here's why.

155
00:07:01,487 --> 00:07:05,825
I could bring in a VIP patient
and a talented surgeon together,

156
00:07:05,892 --> 00:07:06,859
so it's perfect.

157
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,529
Kin-chan isn't a famous doctor!

158
00:07:09,595 --> 00:07:11,664
Let me do the surgery!

159
00:07:11,731 --> 00:07:13,132
Michiko,

160
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:16,536
being a famous doctor
isn't just about having the skills.

161
00:07:17,170 --> 00:07:20,106
Being able to get close to patients
is another great skill.

162
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:24,410
Unless you start to understand
how people feel,

163
00:07:24,477 --> 00:07:25,778
someday…

164
00:07:26,345 --> 00:07:27,613
"Someday" what?

165
00:07:29,582 --> 00:07:31,417
You'll make a mistake.

166
00:07:31,984 --> 00:07:33,352
That's ridiculous.

167
00:07:33,419 --> 00:07:36,088
What happened to you, Akira?
You're acting weird.

168
00:07:40,059 --> 00:07:41,627
What's with him?

169
00:07:41,694 --> 00:07:43,162
Akira!

170
00:07:46,432 --> 00:07:48,768
I hate you!

171
00:07:48,835 --> 00:07:51,204
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

172
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:53,773
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

173
00:08:23,636 --> 00:08:24,470
Hey,

174
00:08:24,537 --> 00:08:26,439
how come you're freelance?

175
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,641
Besides, you're not a famous doctor.

176
00:08:29,408 --> 00:08:32,211
How did you meet Chairman Jake Wang's son?

177
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:34,347
Say something!

178
00:08:35,248 --> 00:08:37,550
Excuse me, but who are you?

179
00:08:37,617 --> 00:08:40,152
What? How can you talk like that?

180
00:08:40,219 --> 00:08:41,821
Oh, I remember.

181
00:08:42,421 --> 00:08:44,657
As long as you returned
to Totei University,

182
00:08:44,724 --> 00:08:46,726
you couldn't care less about anyone else.

183
00:08:46,792 --> 00:08:48,561
You're Dr. Jati, aren't you?

184
00:08:48,628 --> 00:08:49,629
"Jati?"

185
00:08:50,162 --> 00:08:51,497
Dr. Kaji.

186
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:56,669
- Are you angry? I simply--
- No, I'm not angry.

187
00:08:57,236 --> 00:09:00,640
I'm no longer a doctor who sticks
with the crowd and says "Yes, sir."

188
00:09:01,407 --> 00:09:05,511
I'll show you that this is the era
of the freelance doctor.

189
00:09:06,045 --> 00:09:06,946
Goodbye.

190
00:09:09,448 --> 00:09:11,284
He's really ticking me off.

191
00:09:12,351 --> 00:09:14,620
What the heck happened to him?

192
00:09:16,389 --> 00:09:18,558
Ms. Ohma, thank you.

193
00:09:18,624 --> 00:09:21,027
I'll borrow these while I'm here.

194
00:09:22,028 --> 00:09:23,396
Do you have a favorite manga?

195
00:09:25,464 --> 00:09:27,366
<i>Black Jack</i> is a masterpiece.

196
00:09:28,334 --> 00:09:32,638
He's a shadowy doctor who operates
for massive payments.

197
00:09:32,705 --> 00:09:34,473
I love that one, too!

198
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:39,211
If that kind of doctor existed now,
it would be huge trouble.

199
00:09:39,278 --> 00:09:41,981
I can trust a doctor like that more.

200
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:45,418
Real doctors tell nothing but lies.

201
00:09:46,118 --> 00:09:47,853
Even after all the money we paid,

202
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,690
nobody could save my mother.

203
00:09:52,391 --> 00:09:53,459
What?

204
00:09:54,293 --> 00:09:56,529
Do you think there's a super doctor…

205
00:09:57,129 --> 00:09:59,699
who succeeds at every surgery?

206
00:10:02,735 --> 00:10:04,770
In the real world, I don't think so.

207
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:06,806
There is.

208
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:09,342
Really?

209
00:10:10,376 --> 00:10:14,847
Allow me to fill you in
on my patient's condition.

210
00:10:15,381 --> 00:10:18,618
Miroku Oh, age nine.
Hepatoblastoma, PRETEXT two.

211
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:21,721
An eight-centimeter tumor
on the hepatic left lobe.

212
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:24,857
No tumor embolism
or distant metastasis detected.

213
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:27,593
It doesn't appear to be terribly serious.

214
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:30,529
His cancer was discovered
at the Chinese hospital I was at.

215
00:10:30,596 --> 00:10:33,199
Since Miroku's mother is Japanese,

216
00:10:33,265 --> 00:10:36,969
he requested that I operate on him
at a hospital in Japan.

217
00:10:37,036 --> 00:10:39,605
That's enough talking about yourself.

218
00:10:39,672 --> 00:10:42,541
I will remove the tumor
with a left hepatectomy.

219
00:10:42,608 --> 00:10:44,777
- Objection!
- Go ahead, Dr. Daimon.

220
00:10:44,844 --> 00:10:47,179
I have an objection to the surgeon.
I'll do it.

221
00:10:47,246 --> 00:10:49,215
I figured you would say that.

222
00:10:49,281 --> 00:10:51,017
- As for that--
- Objection!

223
00:10:51,584 --> 00:10:53,285
The patient is a nine-year-old boy.

224
00:10:53,352 --> 00:10:54,887
Considering his future growth,

225
00:10:54,954 --> 00:10:57,023
a laparoscopic
partial hepatectomy is best.

226
00:10:57,089 --> 00:11:01,093
No, I believe the addition
of an oncology treatment is best.

227
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:05,264
Surgery after shrinking the tumor
with Cisplatin is less risky.

228
00:11:06,198 --> 00:11:08,034
Well, now, I see.

229
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:08,968
What?

230
00:11:09,035 --> 00:11:12,838
I see very clearly that you
university doctors

231
00:11:12,905 --> 00:11:15,474
who are so busy competing
don't want to allow a freelancer like me

232
00:11:15,541 --> 00:11:17,109
to operate.

233
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:18,878
- What's with this guy?
- You want a fight?

234
00:11:18,944 --> 00:11:21,113
Now, as for an assistant surgeon…

235
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:23,983
Dr. Daimon,

236
00:11:24,050 --> 00:11:25,518
as a fellow member of the agency,

237
00:11:25,584 --> 00:11:26,752
please be my assistant.

238
00:11:26,819 --> 00:11:28,020
I won't.

239
00:11:28,087 --> 00:11:29,655
I figured you would say that.

240
00:11:30,256 --> 00:11:31,657
I guess I have no choice.

241
00:11:31,724 --> 00:11:35,761
Out of respect for your skills,
you can do some of the surgery.

242
00:11:35,828 --> 00:11:37,396
I don't want that. I'll do all of it.

243
00:11:37,463 --> 00:11:39,432
Why don't you want to operate with me?

244
00:11:39,498 --> 00:11:40,866
Because you're annoying!

245
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:44,503
Then allow me to be
your assistant surgeon, Dr. Hara.

246
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:47,306
I have done this surgery
while I was in New York.

247
00:11:47,907 --> 00:11:51,944
I heard that you were of service
at a New York hospital.

248
00:11:52,011 --> 00:11:53,345
He wasn't of any service.

249
00:11:53,412 --> 00:11:56,182
Allow me to handle some
or even half the surgery.

250
00:12:00,486 --> 00:12:01,487
All right.

251
00:12:02,288 --> 00:12:04,490
Rather than a doctor
who clings to his position,

252
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:07,860
I feel empathy with a doctor
who has worked abroad.

253
00:12:07,927 --> 00:12:12,064
Then let me and you, Dr. Korogi,
perform this surgery.

254
00:12:12,131 --> 00:12:13,466
Objection!

255
00:12:13,532 --> 00:12:15,167
It's 5 p.m., so I'll be going.

256
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:17,436
- Hey, troublemaker. Objection!
- We're through.

257
00:12:17,503 --> 00:12:20,473
- We're through.
- Hey, you! We are not through!

258
00:12:20,539 --> 00:12:23,509
<i>I've had it with that jerk!</i>

259
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:25,644
What is he so cocky for?

260
00:12:25,711 --> 00:12:28,514
You guys don't get it.

261
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:31,650
When Dr. Ebina and I
were called back to Totei University,

262
00:12:31,717 --> 00:12:34,286
we naturally intended
to call him back, too.

263
00:12:34,353 --> 00:12:38,390
I completely thought
Dr. Ebina had contacted him,

264
00:12:38,457 --> 00:12:40,826
and he thought I had contacted him.

265
00:12:40,893 --> 00:12:44,230
Then before we knew it,
the position was already filled.

266
00:12:44,797 --> 00:12:47,700
That's when we said, "Oh, well!"

267
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:51,504
It's no wonder Dr. Hara is upset.

268
00:12:51,570 --> 00:12:53,906
You and Dr. Hara
were such good friends, too.

269
00:12:53,973 --> 00:12:57,843
This is your fault, Dr. Kaji.
It's not Dr. Ebina's fault at all!

270
00:12:57,910 --> 00:12:59,612
What? Are you in love with Dr. Ebina?

271
00:12:59,678 --> 00:13:01,647
Actually, that's right!

272
00:13:03,082 --> 00:13:05,551
You're one happy guy, Gengoro.

273
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:13,025
Another, please!

274
00:13:13,092 --> 00:13:15,161
You're drinking awfully fast, Ms. Ohma.

275
00:13:15,227 --> 00:13:16,829
Excuse me. Sashimi, please.

276
00:13:16,896 --> 00:13:17,897
What?

277
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:19,231
It's Dr. Korogi!

278
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:26,038
You come to this kind of place, too,
Dr. Korogi?

279
00:13:26,105 --> 00:13:26,939
Yes.

280
00:13:27,006 --> 00:13:29,542
I sometimes like a little Japanese food.

281
00:13:29,608 --> 00:13:30,810
Oh, give me a break.

282
00:13:35,781 --> 00:13:37,783
Am I in Surgery or Internal Medicine?

283
00:13:38,350 --> 00:13:43,255
Nobody understands how brutal it is
in this peculiar position I'm in!

284
00:13:44,056 --> 00:13:45,624
I'll admit,

285
00:13:45,691 --> 00:13:48,694
it was like a warzone
at that New York hospital.

286
00:13:48,761 --> 00:13:49,895
But in a way,

287
00:13:49,962 --> 00:13:54,333
the everyday stress here
is absolutely brutal!

288
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:59,104
The other day,
Chief Hachisuka called me an idiot!

289
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:01,941
That's abuse of authority.

290
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:03,242
Oh, I know!

291
00:14:03,309 --> 00:14:07,646
I totally know how it is to have
an unreasonable superior.

292
00:14:07,713 --> 00:14:09,582
Poor Dr. Korogi.

293
00:14:09,648 --> 00:14:10,950
Don't fall in love.

294
00:14:16,422 --> 00:14:18,490
You're so pathetic!

295
00:14:20,459 --> 00:14:24,496
That little kid doesn't collapse
under the pressure of being heir

296
00:14:24,563 --> 00:14:27,299
to that huge corporation.

297
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:31,570
But you guys can't even deal
with the minor demands of your bosses.

298
00:14:31,637 --> 00:14:33,105
You're pathetic.

299
00:14:33,172 --> 00:14:35,474
- Her eyes are glazed over.
- Dr. Korogi!

300
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:37,710
Dr. Kaji!

301
00:14:37,776 --> 00:14:39,445
If you don't like it,

302
00:14:39,511 --> 00:14:42,348
then become a more dependable doctor.

303
00:14:42,414 --> 00:14:43,349
What a nasty drunk.

304
00:14:45,918 --> 00:14:46,852
You're right!

305
00:14:47,753 --> 00:14:49,588
- Thank you!
- What?

306
00:14:49,655 --> 00:14:50,789
That's why,

307
00:14:51,323 --> 00:14:53,626
while Chief Hachisuka is away,

308
00:14:53,692 --> 00:14:59,098
I volunteered for that surgery
to redeem myself even a little.

309
00:14:59,164 --> 00:15:00,733
- Yes.
- However…

310
00:15:02,768 --> 00:15:09,308
I'm not so sure I can trust
that surgeon Mamoru Hara.

311
00:15:09,375 --> 00:15:10,509
Don't you dare.

312
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:13,112
Don't trust that shallow four-eyes.

313
00:15:13,879 --> 00:15:15,714
- Yes.
- I'll be honest with you.

314
00:15:16,215 --> 00:15:19,585
A co-worker I had in New York

315
00:15:19,652 --> 00:15:21,820
is at a hospital in Shanghai now.

316
00:15:23,455 --> 00:15:27,693
They told me
something troubling about Dr. Hara.

317
00:15:30,663 --> 00:15:32,364
<i>Pa wan, tsui!</i>

318
00:15:33,165 --> 00:15:34,133
Hey,

319
00:15:34,199 --> 00:15:36,502
what the heck is Kin-chan doing here?

320
00:15:36,568 --> 00:15:38,837
Why not? I'm a member of this agency.

321
00:15:38,904 --> 00:15:40,139
Really?

322
00:15:40,205 --> 00:15:41,407
<i>Pon!</i>

323
00:15:42,508 --> 00:15:44,043
Another great hand again?

324
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:47,012
He has improved in mahjong while in China.

325
00:15:47,079 --> 00:15:50,382
By comparison, Michiko,
you never improve at all.

326
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:52,384
Leave me be!

327
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:55,487
You know, I never expected Akira
to find you, Mamoru Hara,

328
00:15:55,554 --> 00:15:57,389
when he was out scouting.

329
00:15:57,456 --> 00:16:00,759
When Chairman Jake Wang
got his physical exam in China,

330
00:16:00,826 --> 00:16:05,931
I happened to spot his gallbladder polyp.

331
00:16:05,998 --> 00:16:10,336
He ended up liking me
and asked me to do Miroku's surgery.

332
00:16:10,402 --> 00:16:13,505
That's when Mr. Kambara showed up.
It was quite a surprise.

333
00:16:13,572 --> 00:16:15,107
It must be rough for Miroku.

334
00:16:15,174 --> 00:16:16,976
First, he has lost his mom to cancer,

335
00:16:17,042 --> 00:16:18,143
then he got cancer, too.

336
00:16:18,210 --> 00:16:20,279
He's a tough kid.

337
00:16:20,346 --> 00:16:23,983
<i>I heard he didn't cry a single tear</i>
<i>when his mother died.</i>

338
00:16:24,049 --> 00:16:27,820
<i>He has been educated in leadership</i>
<i>by his father since he was little.</i>

339
00:16:27,886 --> 00:16:31,123
<i>He already understands</i>
<i>what his own position is.</i>

340
00:16:31,190 --> 00:16:34,560
I'm wondering if hepatoblastoma
is all that boy really has.

341
00:16:35,527 --> 00:16:38,597
- What do you mean?
- His high CA19-9 count bothers me.

342
00:16:39,898 --> 00:16:41,333
Did you run tests?

343
00:16:42,301 --> 00:16:43,469
Yes, I did.

344
00:16:43,535 --> 00:16:47,373
You refused to assist,
so I don't need your concern.

345
00:16:48,874 --> 00:16:49,775
Akira,

346
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:52,177
if you leave that boy to Kin-chan,
he'll die.

347
00:16:52,244 --> 00:16:53,345
I'm not "Kin-chan"!

348
00:16:53,412 --> 00:16:54,480
It's Mamoru Hara!

349
00:16:54,546 --> 00:16:55,481
No, Kin-chan!

350
00:16:55,547 --> 00:16:56,382
Mamoru Hara!

351
00:16:56,448 --> 00:16:58,984
- Kin-chan!
- Shut up! Enough of that!

352
00:16:59,051 --> 00:17:01,353
- Quit acting like children!
<i>- Ron!</i>

353
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:03,622
One suit and honor tiles.

354
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:06,191
- I've had it with you, Kin-chan!
- It's Mamoru Hara!

355
00:17:06,258 --> 00:17:07,092
Wait!

356
00:17:07,159 --> 00:17:08,961
You're waiting for the three.

357
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:10,629
Ms. Daimon discarded the two.

358
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:12,398
- What?
- Fault!

359
00:17:12,464 --> 00:17:14,633
- Fault!
- Fault!

360
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,934
- What have I done?
- Fault!

361
00:17:16,001 --> 00:17:17,002
- Kin-chan!
- Fault!

362
00:17:17,069 --> 00:17:19,505
- Here, Akira.
- Thank you.

363
00:17:19,571 --> 00:17:21,273
- You're welcome.
- Thanks.

364
00:17:23,075 --> 00:17:24,810
SCALPEL!

365
00:17:27,112 --> 00:17:28,847
Thank you.

366
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:36,889
Hello.

367
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:38,724
Hey,

368
00:17:39,258 --> 00:17:40,793
let's run some tests.

369
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:44,663
Get permission from Dr. Hara.

370
00:17:50,536 --> 00:17:51,770
Listen.

371
00:17:53,439 --> 00:17:56,075
When you're talking to someone,
look them in the eye.

372
00:18:02,514 --> 00:18:04,116
I bet you don't have any friends.

373
00:18:04,183 --> 00:18:05,284
Dr. Daimon!

374
00:18:06,985 --> 00:18:09,088
You're not one to talk.

375
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:13,459
I want to check your bile duct
and for vascular anomalies,

376
00:18:13,525 --> 00:18:15,227
so let's do an MRI.

377
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:19,598
Doctor, what is your name?

378
00:18:19,665 --> 00:18:21,200
Mine?

379
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:23,569
I'm surgeon Michiko Daimon.

380
00:18:23,635 --> 00:18:26,171
If Dr. Hara says it's all right,
I'll get tested.

381
00:18:29,208 --> 00:18:33,812
Dr. Hara isn't like other doctors.
He can make miracles happen.

382
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:37,549
Miracles won't cure your disease.

383
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:39,051
Dr. Daimon, be tactful!

384
00:18:39,885 --> 00:18:43,522
Dr. Hara was chosen by my father.

385
00:18:44,089 --> 00:18:47,426
My disease is already
a subject of interest in China.

386
00:18:48,227 --> 00:18:50,696
Everyone expects me to be cured quickly.

387
00:18:52,331 --> 00:18:53,565
You know what?

388
00:18:54,766 --> 00:18:56,735
You say it's for your father…

389
00:18:58,237 --> 00:18:59,838
and for everyone else.

390
00:19:02,074 --> 00:19:03,709
Who do you want to get better for?

391
00:19:06,645 --> 00:19:08,480
It's your life, you know.

392
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:13,018
Anyway, let's get you tested.

393
00:19:14,353 --> 00:19:16,255
The light will be very bright.

394
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:19,658
Next, the other eye.

395
00:19:23,495 --> 00:19:25,564
EYE EXAMINATION RESULTS

396
00:19:29,434 --> 00:19:32,237
Dr. Hara, come here. We need to talk.

397
00:19:32,304 --> 00:19:33,705
I'm busy. We'll talk later.

398
00:19:33,772 --> 00:19:35,641
- Hey. Dr. Hara.
- Dr. Korogi, let's talk about--

399
00:19:35,707 --> 00:19:36,642
Dr. Hara!

400
00:19:38,410 --> 00:19:41,346
I heard you walked out of two surgeries

401
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:43,649
at that hospital in China.

402
00:19:44,883 --> 00:19:46,785
You're not a great surgeon,

403
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:49,488
but you would never walk out of a surgery.

404
00:19:49,555 --> 00:19:50,889
What happened?

405
00:19:52,391 --> 00:19:54,026
That sure is rude.

406
00:19:54,092 --> 00:19:55,227
Forget that.

407
00:19:55,294 --> 00:19:57,196
Have you decided to apologize to me yet?

408
00:19:57,262 --> 00:19:58,363
Don't change the subject!

409
00:19:58,430 --> 00:19:59,565
If you don't answer me,

410
00:19:59,631 --> 00:20:01,800
I'll tell Acting Director Hiruma about it

411
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:03,702
and have you removed as his doctor.

412
00:20:05,437 --> 00:20:08,373
Do you really want that VIP
for yourself that badly?

413
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:10,242
Cut that out. Tell me what happened.

414
00:20:11,109 --> 00:20:12,678
- Tell me!
- Shut up!

415
00:20:16,448 --> 00:20:17,683
I'll give you an answer.

416
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:19,885
I left during the surgeries…

417
00:20:21,086 --> 00:20:23,655
because while I was operating,

418
00:20:23,722 --> 00:20:26,592
I realized the patient couldn't pay
what they promised to pay.

419
00:20:27,326 --> 00:20:29,561
An ordinary doctor
would be enough for them.

420
00:20:29,628 --> 00:20:30,862
How can you say that?

421
00:20:31,597 --> 00:20:33,365
That won't be a problem with him.

422
00:20:33,432 --> 00:20:35,634
In exchange for an enormous payment,

423
00:20:35,701 --> 00:20:38,237
I'm providing my surgical skills.

424
00:20:38,904 --> 00:20:40,305
My skills are worth it.

425
00:20:40,372 --> 00:20:42,374
What the heck happened to you?

426
00:20:43,008 --> 00:20:45,010
Noboru Hara used to care
about his patients!

427
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:46,678
It's "Mamoru." Goodbye.

428
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:48,647
Wait right there!

429
00:20:48,714 --> 00:20:49,648
Hey!

430
00:20:49,715 --> 00:20:51,083
What's your problem?

431
00:20:51,149 --> 00:20:53,819
Dr. Kaji! Stop it! Don't!

432
00:20:54,853 --> 00:20:58,090
- Dr. Daimon! There's trouble!
- There sure is. It's a collision.

433
00:20:58,156 --> 00:20:59,124
Dr. Hara and Dr. Kaji--

434
00:20:59,191 --> 00:21:00,459
Not that.

435
00:21:00,525 --> 00:21:01,693
It's a collision tumor.

436
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,629
- Collision tumor?
- Collision tumor?

437
00:21:03,695 --> 00:21:05,297
- Collision tumor?
- Collision tumor?

438
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:09,868
A collision tumor?

439
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:13,338
Yes. Here are the results
of the tests that Dr. Daimon ran.

440
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:17,609
Besides the hepatoblastoma,
there's a tumor on the bile duct.

441
00:21:17,676 --> 00:21:19,745
- The two tumors have collided.
- I see.

442
00:21:19,811 --> 00:21:22,614
What's more, they're surrounding
the main portal vein.

443
00:21:23,682 --> 00:21:24,683
In this condition,

444
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:26,551
he cannot be operated on.

445
00:21:27,352 --> 00:21:30,289
If anything were to happen
to Chairman Jake Wang's son,

446
00:21:30,355 --> 00:21:32,691
the hospital would be held responsible.

447
00:21:33,825 --> 00:21:35,794
Well, if he can't be operated …

448
00:21:37,362 --> 00:21:39,965
then we'll just have to…

449
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:44,670
send Miroku Oh back to China.

450
00:21:44,736 --> 00:21:46,471
That's for the best.

451
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,207
You're kidding…

452
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:52,978
We'll send Miroku Oh…

453
00:21:54,112 --> 00:21:57,616
back to China.

454
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,285
Okay?

455
00:22:00,352 --> 00:22:01,720
Answer me.

456
00:22:02,888 --> 00:22:03,955
Yes, sir.

457
00:22:09,227 --> 00:22:10,595
Yes, sir.

458
00:22:12,264 --> 00:22:13,598
Dr. Hara?

459
00:22:17,936 --> 00:22:19,671
- Yes, sir.
- Good.

460
00:22:22,607 --> 00:22:23,809
<i>I see.</i>

461
00:22:24,543 --> 00:22:26,745
My disease is that bad, is it?

462
00:22:30,649 --> 00:22:31,683
But…

463
00:22:32,851 --> 00:22:35,020
you can do the surgery, right, Dr. Hara?

464
00:22:41,893 --> 00:22:42,794
I am Mamoru Hara.

465
00:22:42,861 --> 00:22:43,795
CHINA, ONE MONTH EARLIER

466
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:46,732
I was a surgeon
at Totei University Hospital in Japan.

467
00:22:46,798 --> 00:22:48,400
It's nice to meet you.

468
00:22:48,467 --> 00:22:49,668
Totei University?

469
00:22:51,236 --> 00:22:53,905
That's the hospital that performed
synovial sarcoma removal

470
00:22:53,972 --> 00:22:56,541
alongside autologous
chondrocyte implantation.

471
00:22:56,608 --> 00:22:58,443
Oh, wow! How come you know that?

472
00:23:00,045 --> 00:23:01,713
It was on the Internet.

473
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:02,914
I see.

474
00:23:04,149 --> 00:23:06,218
That was a difficult surgery.

475
00:23:06,284 --> 00:23:09,721
It usually takes six hours,
but we finished it in three.

476
00:23:10,288 --> 00:23:12,424
- Did you do it?
- Well, yes.

477
00:23:12,924 --> 00:23:16,294
- The surgeon was Dr. Daimon…
- The first time ever.

478
00:23:16,361 --> 00:23:19,898
It was big news in the medical world.

479
00:23:19,965 --> 00:23:22,200
"Live donor domino transplant."

480
00:23:22,267 --> 00:23:23,602
Oh, the one in Cuba.

481
00:23:24,369 --> 00:23:26,304
That brings back memories.

482
00:23:26,371 --> 00:23:28,940
You've done surgeries overseas, too?

483
00:23:29,007 --> 00:23:30,575
Yes. Well…

484
00:23:31,109 --> 00:23:33,278
I never make mistakes.

485
00:23:37,349 --> 00:23:38,617
That was a lie, wasn't it?

486
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:42,320
I accidentally…

487
00:23:44,723 --> 00:23:48,794
misled you into believing
that I am an amazing surgeon.

488
00:23:50,796 --> 00:23:53,765
Then when your father,
Chairman Wang, put his trust in me,

489
00:23:56,601 --> 00:23:57,969
I couldn't tell you the truth.

490
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,308
I wanted to cure you.

491
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:05,811
I was confident that I could.

492
00:24:07,379 --> 00:24:09,514
So I tried to become a super doctor.

493
00:24:12,217 --> 00:24:13,218
But…

494
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:16,788
I couldn't do it.

495
00:24:22,260 --> 00:24:23,361
I am sorry.

496
00:24:55,460 --> 00:24:57,762
When did your vision start going bad?

497
00:24:58,530 --> 00:25:00,398
EYE EXAMINATION RESULTS

498
00:25:00,465 --> 00:25:04,436
I bet you left during surgery
in that Chinese hospital…

499
00:25:06,137 --> 00:25:07,472
because of that, huh?

500
00:25:13,311 --> 00:25:14,679
Normally, I see just fine.

501
00:25:16,448 --> 00:25:20,685
But as soon as I get into surgery…

502
00:25:21,286 --> 00:25:24,356
Next, we'll do the tunneling.

503
00:25:24,422 --> 00:25:25,690
Kelly clamp.

504
00:25:34,065 --> 00:25:35,667
Dr. Hara, are you okay?

505
00:25:36,935 --> 00:25:38,136
<i>I got vision tests…</i>

506
00:25:38,637 --> 00:25:40,372
and neurological tests.

507
00:25:41,907 --> 00:25:43,475
But there was nothing wrong.

508
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:49,881
So you don't know the cause.

509
00:25:51,616 --> 00:25:54,486
How can you go into surgery like that?

510
00:25:58,790 --> 00:26:00,592
You're not fit to be a physician.

511
00:26:09,801 --> 00:26:10,769
I know.

512
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:16,274
I figured…

513
00:26:18,710 --> 00:26:21,780
if I came here, I could get
Dr. Daimon's cooperation.

514
00:26:27,285 --> 00:26:28,587
As long as…

515
00:26:30,622 --> 00:26:32,157
Miroku could be cured…

516
00:26:33,825 --> 00:26:34,960
That's all I wanted.

517
00:26:38,663 --> 00:26:39,798
But even that…

518
00:26:44,469 --> 00:26:45,470
I…

519
00:26:50,475 --> 00:26:52,043
will quit as a surgeon.

520
00:26:56,081 --> 00:26:57,015
Thanks for this.

521
00:27:06,558 --> 00:27:09,294
These two tumors
are really quite a problem.

522
00:27:09,361 --> 00:27:10,195
Yes.

523
00:27:13,632 --> 00:27:14,899
Hey, Akira,

524
00:27:15,433 --> 00:27:17,802
why did you bring Kin-chan here?

525
00:27:17,869 --> 00:27:19,671
Isn't it obvious?

526
00:27:19,738 --> 00:27:21,940
By bringing them a patient and a doctor,

527
00:27:22,007 --> 00:27:24,109
I can bill Totei University for a bundle.

528
00:27:24,175 --> 00:27:25,644
Is that all?

529
00:27:25,710 --> 00:27:27,746
- What do you mean?
- Are you hiding something?

530
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:29,414
Don't be ridiculous.

531
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:33,818
Lately, you're always going out.
I have no idea what you're doing.

532
00:27:33,885 --> 00:27:35,420
Sales. I'm doing sales.

533
00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:36,821
And I'm scouting.

534
00:27:37,322 --> 00:27:38,890
I'm very busy, you know.

535
00:27:45,897 --> 00:27:47,232
Miroku.

536
00:27:48,133 --> 00:27:50,802
Did you get permission to go out tonight?

537
00:27:56,141 --> 00:27:57,042
Come on in.

538
00:27:57,575 --> 00:27:59,210
What's the matter?

539
00:28:05,116 --> 00:28:06,785
I can have anything I wish…

540
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:10,221
but I am not free.

541
00:28:11,990 --> 00:28:13,625
I'm jealous of you, Dr. Daimon,

542
00:28:14,759 --> 00:28:16,695
since you can do as you please.

543
00:28:20,832 --> 00:28:22,267
Why, thank you.

544
00:28:24,536 --> 00:28:25,670
Unlike Dr. Hara,

545
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:29,574
you don't flatter with lies…

546
00:28:30,675 --> 00:28:31,976
or try to be friendly.

547
00:28:32,644 --> 00:28:36,247
- Did you come to pick a fight?
- That's why I came to talk to you!

548
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:40,852
Dr. Daimon.

549
00:28:43,288 --> 00:28:44,589
Can I be cured?

550
00:28:51,129 --> 00:28:52,530
With my mother,

551
00:28:53,231 --> 00:28:56,601
I trusted the doctors
when they said they could cure her.

552
00:28:58,737 --> 00:28:59,771
But…

553
00:29:01,206 --> 00:29:02,774
a miracle never happened.

554
00:29:09,714 --> 00:29:10,815
I…

555
00:29:12,817 --> 00:29:14,119
want to live!

556
00:29:31,369 --> 00:29:32,337
Listen.

557
00:29:34,072 --> 00:29:36,307
Miracles don't happen in surgery.

558
00:29:41,513 --> 00:29:43,448
But I can cure you.

559
00:29:46,484 --> 00:29:47,385
Is that the truth?

560
00:29:49,854 --> 00:29:52,123
Like you said, I don't lie.

561
00:29:52,924 --> 00:29:53,825
Then…

562
00:29:55,326 --> 00:29:56,828
I will disobey my father.

563
00:29:57,829 --> 00:29:58,963
It's my life,

564
00:29:59,497 --> 00:30:00,865
so I'll make the decision.

565
00:30:03,101 --> 00:30:04,302
I want you…

566
00:30:05,703 --> 00:30:07,605
to come to China and do my operation.

567
00:30:10,141 --> 00:30:12,043
You didn't have to ask.
I already intended to.

568
00:30:12,110 --> 00:30:13,244
Right, Akira?

569
00:30:13,311 --> 00:30:15,513
My agency did accept this job,

570
00:30:16,047 --> 00:30:19,284
so we'll take care of you
until the very end.

571
00:30:19,350 --> 00:30:20,285
However,

572
00:30:20,351 --> 00:30:24,189
we don't go anywhere
unless it's by first class.

573
00:30:24,689 --> 00:30:25,790
Also…

574
00:30:26,558 --> 00:30:28,593
Get us super-high-class Chinese meals.

575
00:30:29,227 --> 00:30:30,795
Of course.

576
00:30:30,862 --> 00:30:33,364
And the hotel.
Get us the best hotel there is.

577
00:30:33,431 --> 00:30:35,733
Oh, and pandas. Show us lots of pandas.

578
00:30:56,821 --> 00:30:57,822
Dr. Hara,

579
00:30:58,356 --> 00:30:59,557
I appreciate all you've done.

580
00:31:01,326 --> 00:31:05,196
I will be operated on
by a Japanese surgeon in China.

581
00:31:08,733 --> 00:31:12,170
I am grateful that you and I became close.

582
00:31:14,739 --> 00:31:15,707
Miroku…

583
00:31:25,617 --> 00:31:26,684
- Miroku!
- Miroku!

584
00:31:26,751 --> 00:31:29,687
- Call someone! And get a stretcher!
- Got it!

585
00:31:29,754 --> 00:31:31,222
Stay with me, Miroku!

586
00:31:33,291 --> 00:31:35,793
The hepatoblastoma may have ruptured.

587
00:31:35,860 --> 00:31:39,330
Miroku, can you hear me?
You'll be all right!

588
00:31:39,397 --> 00:31:40,765
Dr. Hara, what will we do?

589
00:31:42,867 --> 00:31:45,136
- I'll perform emergency surgery.
- Okay.

590
00:31:45,203 --> 00:31:46,037
Dr. Hara!

591
00:31:46,104 --> 00:31:48,206
Prep the OR and ultrasound immediately!

592
00:31:48,273 --> 00:31:49,474
Yes, sir!

593
00:31:51,409 --> 00:31:52,577
Miroku?

594
00:31:52,644 --> 00:31:53,978
He's going into emergency surgery.

595
00:31:54,045 --> 00:31:55,580
The surgeon will be Dr. Hara.

596
00:31:56,147 --> 00:31:57,815
Dr. Hara can't perform that operation!

597
00:31:57,882 --> 00:31:59,951
- But wait!
- Hang on!

598
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:02,487
If any of us even touch this surgery,

599
00:32:03,488 --> 00:32:04,422
we'll be fired.

600
00:32:12,530 --> 00:32:15,533
INTERNATIONAL FLIGHTS

601
00:32:24,575 --> 00:32:27,345
Oh, damn it! Crap!

602
00:32:30,281 --> 00:32:31,716
This is from Dr. Daimon.

603
00:32:33,351 --> 00:32:34,352
From Dr. Daimon?

604
00:32:34,986 --> 00:32:35,820
Don't worry.

605
00:32:35,887 --> 00:32:37,088
I'll operate with you.

606
00:32:37,588 --> 00:32:40,425
Let's save Miroku's life together.

607
00:32:41,559 --> 00:32:42,694
Dr. Kaji…

608
00:32:43,895 --> 00:32:44,929
Wash up again.

609
00:32:59,077 --> 00:33:00,945
Dr. Jonouchi, where's Demon?

610
00:33:01,012 --> 00:33:04,849
She said she's going far away to operate,
but that's all I know.

611
00:33:09,687 --> 00:33:11,055
We will now conduct

612
00:33:11,122 --> 00:33:15,526
a caudate lobectomy and hepatic
lateral segmentectomy on Miroku Oh.

613
00:33:15,593 --> 00:33:19,263
BP 98 over 65, pulse 87, normal sinus.

614
00:33:20,131 --> 00:33:20,999
- Scalpel.
- Here.

615
00:33:21,065 --> 00:33:22,567
Hooked forceps.

616
00:33:32,410 --> 00:33:33,711
Bovie.

617
00:33:37,148 --> 00:33:38,449
Dr. Kaji…

618
00:33:40,952 --> 00:33:43,121
SURGERY TIME

619
00:33:48,226 --> 00:33:50,895
His left hepatic artery is around here.

620
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:54,532
- Be careful.
- I will.

621
00:33:58,036 --> 00:33:59,804
- Ablating the caudate lobe. Pean.
- Here.

622
00:34:09,714 --> 00:34:12,150
The tumor has accreted
to the inferior vena cava.

623
00:34:14,085 --> 00:34:15,887
This is trickier than expected.

624
00:34:19,090 --> 00:34:20,658
Dr. Hara, Dr. Kaji.

625
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:22,994
That tumor cannot be removed.

626
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:24,595
End this surgery.

627
00:34:32,603 --> 00:34:33,538
Are you all right?

628
00:34:35,573 --> 00:34:36,774
I'm fine. I can see.

629
00:34:39,877 --> 00:34:40,945
If we end this now,

630
00:34:41,012 --> 00:34:42,280
Miroku can't be saved.

631
00:34:43,414 --> 00:34:46,150
I promised him I would save him.

632
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,554
I don't want to lie anymore.

633
00:34:55,193 --> 00:34:56,594
- Sweat.
- Right.

634
00:35:05,903 --> 00:35:07,038
It's not good.

635
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:09,373
The accretion is so severe,
we can't go further.

636
00:35:09,874 --> 00:35:12,710
Let's block the inferior vena cava
with the TVE method.

637
00:35:13,511 --> 00:35:17,215
But that will aggravate blood flow
and destabilize circulation.

638
00:35:17,281 --> 00:35:19,117
Let's use the IVC half clamping method.

639
00:35:19,183 --> 00:35:20,485
TVE is clearly better!

640
00:35:20,551 --> 00:35:21,786
There's no time for arguing!

641
00:35:23,521 --> 00:35:25,356
We'll use the IVC half clamping method.

642
00:35:25,423 --> 00:35:26,591
- DeBakey clamp!
- Here.

643
00:35:38,936 --> 00:35:40,171
BP down to 68!

644
00:35:40,238 --> 00:35:42,073
Fissure in inferior vena cava.

645
00:35:42,874 --> 00:35:45,343
- Dr. Hara, want me to take over?
- I'm fine.

646
00:35:45,409 --> 00:35:47,445
- I'll fix this. Another DeBakey!
- Here.

647
00:36:12,603 --> 00:36:13,771
Dr. Daimon!

648
00:36:13,838 --> 00:36:15,306
I'm finally here.

649
00:36:15,373 --> 00:36:16,207
Out of the way.

650
00:36:19,343 --> 00:36:21,579
- IVC block. Fogarty clamp.
- Here.

651
00:36:27,718 --> 00:36:29,053
Hold this.

652
00:36:30,955 --> 00:36:32,623
Damaged location found.

653
00:36:32,690 --> 00:36:34,358
- 4-0 monofilament.
- Here.

654
00:36:34,992 --> 00:36:35,993
Demon,

655
00:36:36,060 --> 00:36:38,329
this tumor is in a very tricky spot.

656
00:36:38,396 --> 00:36:40,731
Total removal will be tough even for you.

657
00:36:40,798 --> 00:36:42,333
Let me do this.

658
00:36:43,034 --> 00:36:45,803
Thanks to those eye drops
you gave me, I can see.

659
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:48,005
Those were just drops for dry eyes.

660
00:36:48,072 --> 00:36:50,074
- But…
- The placebo effect, huh?

661
00:36:50,875 --> 00:36:52,944
It's psychogenic blindness.

662
00:36:53,010 --> 00:36:55,780
You were putting too much pressure
on yourself.

663
00:36:58,115 --> 00:37:00,017
You really are so naive.

664
00:37:00,084 --> 00:37:01,619
What?

665
00:37:02,987 --> 00:37:05,323
SURGERY TIME

666
00:37:11,195 --> 00:37:13,598
BP not climbing out of the 70s.

667
00:37:15,132 --> 00:37:16,267
It's not good.

668
00:37:16,334 --> 00:37:18,202
We can't get to the tumor.

669
00:37:20,605 --> 00:37:21,739
We'll detach the liver.

670
00:37:21,806 --> 00:37:24,108
- Surgical ultrasound and Belgetty clamp.
- Here.

671
00:37:24,175 --> 00:37:27,311
You can't hang the liver
from the inferior vena cava!

672
00:37:27,378 --> 00:37:30,648
It's hard to see and any more
hemorrhaging is dangerous.

673
00:37:30,715 --> 00:37:33,384
Can even you do that, Dr. Daimon?

674
00:37:42,426 --> 00:37:44,695
Doesn't pressure affect you?

675
00:37:45,963 --> 00:37:47,765
All surgeries are full of pressure.

676
00:37:54,071 --> 00:37:55,539
I…

677
00:37:56,040 --> 00:37:57,675
want to live!

678
00:38:01,846 --> 00:38:05,249
I… will not fail.

679
00:38:20,931 --> 00:38:23,267
Taping complete. Lift it.

680
00:38:25,636 --> 00:38:26,671
Here goes.

681
00:38:28,039 --> 00:38:29,907
- Very carefully.
- Right.

682
00:38:32,410 --> 00:38:34,478
<i>A doctor who makes miracles happen?</i>

683
00:38:34,545 --> 00:38:37,214
<i>Does one really exist?</i>

684
00:38:38,115 --> 00:38:39,550
Somewhere in the world…

685
00:38:44,422 --> 00:38:45,489
there is one.

686
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:12,383
Blood pressure
and central venous pressure stable.

687
00:39:13,617 --> 00:39:15,286
Let's remove both these tumors.

688
00:39:15,353 --> 00:39:17,355
Restarting liver detachment. Pean.

689
00:39:39,777 --> 00:39:44,048
BP 95 over 68, pulse 81, normal sinus.

690
00:39:45,816 --> 00:39:47,017
We're done.

691
00:39:49,487 --> 00:39:50,988
We did it!

692
00:39:51,055 --> 00:39:52,757
Thank goodness.

693
00:40:00,698 --> 00:40:04,135
First-class seats and Chinese food.
I'm counting on it.

694
00:40:04,635 --> 00:40:05,970
Nice work.

695
00:40:06,036 --> 00:40:07,471
- Nice work.
- Nice work.

696
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:10,374
Dr. Daimon!

697
00:40:12,209 --> 00:40:13,511
Thank you!

698
00:40:34,799 --> 00:40:35,800
Miroku,

699
00:40:36,333 --> 00:40:38,035
how are you feeling?

700
00:40:42,606 --> 00:40:44,475
The surgery was a success.

701
00:40:46,410 --> 00:40:47,378
You'll be fine now.

702
00:40:49,947 --> 00:40:50,915
Thank you.

703
00:40:54,251 --> 00:40:56,720
I knew it was you, Dr. Hara…

704
00:40:59,557 --> 00:41:02,126
Doctor X.

705
00:41:03,861 --> 00:41:05,129
What?

706
00:41:07,832 --> 00:41:11,469
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

707
00:41:13,037 --> 00:41:15,239
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

708
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:20,344
I would like to thank you for employing
Dr. Daimon and Dr. Jonouchi.

709
00:41:20,411 --> 00:41:21,645
This is a melon.

710
00:41:21,712 --> 00:41:24,348
You say we employed them,

711
00:41:24,415 --> 00:41:28,319
but what the two of them did
was without permission.

712
00:41:28,385 --> 00:41:31,121
I hope you understand that.

713
00:41:31,188 --> 00:41:34,925
Chairman Jake Wang has called
to express his thanks.

714
00:41:34,992 --> 00:41:39,196
So I guess we can let it slide this time.

715
00:41:39,263 --> 00:41:41,765
- Then here is the bill.
- Okay.

716
00:41:42,466 --> 00:41:44,034
- Here.
- Let me have a look.

717
00:41:47,104 --> 00:41:48,205
"30,000 yen?"

718
00:41:48,272 --> 00:41:50,674
This is fewer zeroes than usual.

719
00:41:50,741 --> 00:41:53,511
That is the bill for Dr. Hara's share.

720
00:41:55,279 --> 00:41:57,181
To each according to their skills.

721
00:41:57,248 --> 00:42:00,484
- Here is the other bill.
- Okay.

722
00:42:02,887 --> 00:42:05,189
SURGICAL FEES FOR DR. DAIMON

723
00:42:05,256 --> 00:42:07,091
- Thirty million yen!
- That's right.

724
00:42:07,157 --> 00:42:10,027
Since we brought you the patient,

725
00:42:10,094 --> 00:42:12,730
I have added a little bit.

726
00:42:12,796 --> 00:42:13,864
Mr. Kambara.

727
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:16,066
You know what?

728
00:42:16,634 --> 00:42:20,638
For the longest time, there has been
something I've wanted to ask you.

729
00:42:20,704 --> 00:42:24,408
You always charge so much,

730
00:42:25,109 --> 00:42:29,046
but what on Earth do you use it for?

731
00:42:32,049 --> 00:42:35,085
Can I leave that to your imagination?

732
00:42:36,921 --> 00:42:39,590
I can't imagine spending that much.

733
00:42:39,657 --> 00:42:41,225
Then please just pay up.

734
00:42:42,226 --> 00:42:45,329
The Doctor Referral Agency.

735
00:42:45,396 --> 00:42:47,831
really insisted that I stay.

736
00:42:47,898 --> 00:42:51,302
But Totei pleaded to have me.

737
00:42:51,368 --> 00:42:53,237
So I've returned.

738
00:42:53,304 --> 00:42:54,638
Tell the truth!

739
00:42:54,705 --> 00:42:56,640
You're not even a famous doctor anyway!

740
00:42:57,374 --> 00:42:58,375
Good point.

741
00:42:58,442 --> 00:42:59,577
Oh, give me a break.

742
00:42:59,643 --> 00:43:01,178
I've had it with you.

743
00:43:02,680 --> 00:43:04,481
It's nice being in an organization!

744
00:43:04,548 --> 00:43:06,016
"Yes, sir" and hierarchy.

745
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:08,586
No pressure! Stress-free!

746
00:43:08,652 --> 00:43:12,022
Start feeling a little pressure!
You're causing all of us stress!

747
00:43:12,089 --> 00:43:14,191
- Good point.
- What's your problem?

748
00:43:14,258 --> 00:43:18,262
This environment must be one
where Dr. Hara feels secure.

749
00:43:18,862 --> 00:43:21,765
You can't be a surgeon
unless you can overcome pressure.

750
00:43:23,367 --> 00:43:28,205
I forgot to tell you! My pillar!
I feel so close to you!

751
00:43:34,511 --> 00:43:36,547
<i>She hates groups,</i>

752
00:43:37,648 --> 00:43:40,184
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

753
00:43:40,250 --> 00:43:41,919
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

754
00:43:42,853 --> 00:43:46,323
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

755
00:43:46,390 --> 00:43:47,358
<i> to work her way up.</i>

756
00:43:48,058 --> 00:43:49,593
Hey, what's wrong, Demon?

757
00:43:50,260 --> 00:43:52,863
Why do you look so angry, Dr. Daimon?

758
00:43:52,930 --> 00:43:54,231
She always looks that way.

759
00:43:54,298 --> 00:43:55,499
- That's true.
- Move it, Kin-chan

760
00:43:55,566 --> 00:43:57,034
Not "Kin-chan." It's Mamoru Hara!

761
00:43:57,101 --> 00:43:58,369
Why bump into us?

762
00:43:59,436 --> 00:44:01,639
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

763
00:44:01,705 --> 00:44:04,308
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

764
00:44:05,576 --> 00:44:10,180
I am prepared to pay the remaining amount.

765
00:44:11,448 --> 00:44:13,384
Thank you.

766
00:44:14,151 --> 00:44:18,856
Then we can officially conclude
the contract.

767
00:44:20,090 --> 00:44:21,091
Now,

768
00:44:21,625 --> 00:44:25,362
Michiko Daimon is no longer needed, right?

769
00:44:34,038 --> 00:44:38,075
- Superpowered Channel!
<i>- What's this got to do with medicine?</i>

770
00:44:38,142 --> 00:44:40,477
<i>In the future,</i>
<i>a doctor's weapon won't be the scalpel.</i>

771
00:44:40,544 --> 00:44:41,378
<i>It will be influence!</i>

772
00:44:41,445 --> 00:44:43,113
I will never forgive you!

773
00:44:43,180 --> 00:44:44,615
Then go and convince her.

774
00:44:44,682 --> 00:44:46,016
Influence is your weapon, right?

775
00:44:46,083 --> 00:44:47,284
Woah!

776
00:44:47,351 --> 00:44:48,318
A LOVE-HATE RELATIONSHIP?

777
00:44:48,385 --> 00:44:49,386
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
